# A companion cut down in a fight leaves the party, and leaves a body.
#
# Companions could not really die. `CompanionParty.Remove` was reached by the old-age check and by
# the heart-ceiling overflow and by nothing else, so a companion whose hit points hit zero in a fight
# walked out of it at zero hit points and stayed in the party for ever — still counted against the
# heart ceiling, still handed the narration by Speak About, still turning up in the next fight with
# no hit points left to lose.
#
# One funnel answers all three causes now (SettleCompanionDeaths, asking PartyMember.CauseOfDeath
# every tick outside a fight). This script covers the Wounds arm; companion_death_humors.cli and
# companion_death_age.cli cover the other two. Each is asserted separately because only the funnel is
# shared — how each death is arrived at is not.
#
# `fight-wound` exists for this: `fight-end` settles the whole fight and cannot single anybody out,
# and steering the enemy AI onto one party member for long enough to kill them is not something a
# script can ask for. The companion is named because at seed 42 --fill-party gives the cat
# Nighthunter, which companion_handoff.cli already keys on.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only brewer --auto-dialogue

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# The companion is in the party before any of this.
inspect party
expect-state party Nighthunter

strategy succeed
goal attack
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

wait mode Fighting 90

# Kill the companion by wounds — hit points, not humors.
fight-wound Nighthunter
wait 20

# A dead companion must NOT end the fight: the protagonist is still standing, and CheckFightEnd is
# faction arithmetic. Still being in Fighting here is that assertion.
wait mode Fighting 20

fight-end victory
wait 90

# The notice is modal over every mode — including narration, which redraws itself every frame and
# would paint straight over a box gated below the mode dispatch. These two `expect`s scan the
# rendered screen, so they only pass if it really is on top.
expect Nighthunter
expect died of their wounds

click companion-death
wait 60
advance 12 180

# Out of the party for good...
inspect party
expect-no-state party Nighthunter
# ...and a body left where they fell.
inspect pois
expect-state pois Nighthunter's Remains

quit
